# Consumer validation plan

D-01 / R-01: Independent Rust/std evaluation modules in tools/governance/consumers, built with the installed Rust 1.99.1. Use exact bytes rather than a collision-prone substitute for content identity. Ledger uses checked integer units and fixed-offset timezones; context consumes an explicit small source grammar with exact ranges and labeled unresolved calls. Graph requires validated evidence and bounded examined edges. Output preserves original files and separates display/estimates. These are evaluation consumers, not full production engines.
D-02 / R-02: Owned temporary directories, cooperating writers serialized across processes by atomic lock-directory creation, base-byte preconditions, journal/staging and crash injection. Polling watcher treats notification as a hint and reconciles actual reads. Symlink/traversal tests cover static paths in owned trees; hostile concurrent directory replacement and power-loss durability are not claimed. Stream fixture has bounded retained output and observed direct-child/worker cleanup. Publication target is an ephemeral loopback receiver with its own grant check; no external endpoint. Bubblewrap 0.13.1 with private PID/user/network/mount namespaces confines only disposable test plugins; unavailable isolation is never treated as a pass.
D-03 / R-03: Separate Iced 0.14 consumer linked against the installed workspace dependency build. Real event-loop timers, widget focus operations, window resizing and counters observe the four scenarios. Graphical sessions are bounded and exited normally; no product visual claims from state-only tests.
D-04 / R-04: Preserve all prior feature envelopes. Bind concrete consumer/oracle sources, fixtures, compiler/dependency identity, commands, outputs and limitations. New experiments may expose defects; fix within the evaluation scope and retain failed logs. Do not change the 36 original technical scenarios. Reexamine the prior technical-acceptance feature because its evidence explicitly binds skill evidence files.

Primary: .codex/skills/software-testing/SKILL.md (sdd/chain/software-testing.md version 1): independent cases and negative controls. Supporting rust (sdd/chain/rust.md version 1): safe Rust resource ownership; workspace-integrity-engineering (bridge version 1): compare/write and crash recovery; application-security (bridge version 1): host-versus-process isolation and receiver-side publication permission. Entries consulted at their actual .codex/skills/<name>/SKILL.md paths; no declared semantic versions. Content identities in skills.json. The nine evaluated skills/references are evaluation subjects and technical inputs, not nine automatically activated workflows.
